        "__________________________________________________________________________\n",
        "\n",
        "The code snippet below filters the `df` DataFrame to select only entries that meet specific criteria for Jane Austen's novels:\n",
        "\n",
        "1.  **`df['Authors'].str.contains('Austen, Jane', na=False)`**: This checks the 'Authors' column for entries that contain the string 'Austen, Jane'. The `na=False` argument ensures that `NaN` (Not a Number) values in the 'Authors' column are treated as `False` and don't raise an error.\n",
        "2.  **`df['Type'] == 'Text'`**: This filters for entries where the 'Type' column is exactly 'Text', ensuring we're only looking at actual books and not other content types.\n",
        "3.  **`df['Language'] == 'en'`**: This restricts the results to books written in English.\n",
        "\n",
        "These three conditions are combined using the `&` (AND) operator, so only rows that satisfy all three conditions are selected."
