      "metadata": {
        "id": "a73362f5"
      },
      "source": [
        "The previous plot shows the sentiment score for each individual sentence. Since there are many sentences, this can look quite noisy. To get a smoother understanding of the sentiment trajectory, we can average the sentiment scores over segments of a certain number of sentences. This helps to highlight the broader emotional shifts within the narrative."
      ],
      "id": "a73362f5"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "number_of_sentences_per_segment = 10\n",
        "sentiment_scores = list(sentiment_df['Sentiment'])\n",
        "avg_scores = []\n",
        "\n",
        "for i in range(len(sentiment_scores)//number_of_sentences_per_segment):\n",
        "  avg_score = 0\n",
        "  for j in range(number_of_sentences_per_segment):\n",
        "    avg_score += sentiment_scores[i*number_of_sentences_per_segment + j]\n",
        "\n",
        "  avg_score /= number_of_sentences_per_segment\n",
        "\n",
        "  avg_scores.append(avg_score)\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.plot(avg_scores)\n",
        "plt.ylabel('Average Sentiment Score')\n",
        "plt.xlabel('Segment Number')\n",
        "plt.title('Sentiment Analysis of \"TITLE\"')\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
